conductor-sync-selinux: SELinux policy for conductor-sync
=========================================================

The module "conductor_sync" (targeted policy, priority 200) confines
/usr/bin/conductor-sync in conductor_sync_t when systemd starts it
(conductor-sync.service, the scheduled runs, and conductor-sync-api.service,
the management API). Commands an administrator runs by hand
("sudo -u conductor-sync conductor-sync plan") stay in the administrator's
domain.

File types:

  conductor_sync_conf_t     /etc/conductor-sync (conductor-sync.toml, domain CA)
  conductor_sync_cred_t     /etc/conductor-sync/credentials (read by systemd
                            for the services; by the administrator's manual runs)
  conductor_sync_var_lib_t  /var/lib/conductor-sync (links, runs, audit log)
  conductor_sync_var_run_t  /run/conductor-sync (api.sock)

conductor-sync connects to the domain controllers (LDAP/LDAPS, Kerberos)
and to HTTPS (Google's APIs, an optional webhook). conductor (conductor_t)
may use the API socket. A metrics_file outside /var/lib/conductor-sync
needs its own rule (or a path labeled conductor_sync_var_lib_t).

Troubleshooting:

  ausearch -m AVC,USER_AVC -ts recent -c conductor-sync
  semanage permissive -a conductor_sync_t     (and -d to revert)
